DETAILED COMMENTS (to be returned to the author(s))\par
[Reviewers are encouraged to provide substantitive comments \par
supporting their numerical scale ratings. Reviews without \par
such comments may not be considered in the overall rating of the paper.]\par

The authors propose a keyword propagation scheme, which annotates
unlabeled images via relevance feedback.  The scheme is useful.
The following is a list of required changes.

o page 15.  The discussion on the mixture of Gaussian model and
  the use of a region-based approach should be moved to the
  conclusion section.  Placing unsubstantiated conjectures here
  weakens the paper.

o page 16.  The paper should present the names of the 79 Corel 
  categories used by the experiments so that future works can compare
  their results with the results of this paper.  This may take up one 
  additional page, but it is deemed necessary.
  
o page 18.  The x-axis of the figure should be # of rounds in
  integer.  

o page 18, 19.  Please explain why different schemes have different
  accuracy at round #0.  

o page 18-20.  The figures should show more number of iterations.  
  I am in particular interested in seeing if the 2nd line in
  Figure 9 can catch up with the first line with a few more 
  iterations.  If this is indeed the case, please explain the 
  reasons.

o page 21. The claim for superiority should be tuned down.  It
  is adequate to just say that the experimental results show that
  the proposed scheme performs significantly better than some
  traditional CBIR schemes.

o page 21.  The authors are suggested to have a candid discussion
  on the limitations of its current system and planned future work.
  
